Z||000000||SLAMMED87GT||11-27-2001||11:59 PM||||Well, right now I am good because I did get my first Beretta rear brakes done. BTW- It's related to the Fiero because that is the car I looked at through the window while I was stuck in the garage with the Beretta!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I noticed a real change in braking performance the other day on the way home. Basically like the pedal went to the floor! Well, upon taking the drums off I noticed something. Yah, something like =brake fluid and shreds of the pad, well maybe I should say barily any pad! The wheel cylinder had blown up and thats why my braking was bad. It was a mess! Brake fluid all over the springs, pads, cylinder. Anyways, the other one must not hav worked for a long time. It is bone DRY! Like rusty dry! The pads barily moved around. I believe the wheel cylinder in that one is frozen.<P>So I bought new shoes, wheel cylinders, and brake fluid. After I figured out how put the damn thing together it was fine!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>I want drive my Fiero, yah and monkeys might fly out of my butt! How about 8 inches of snow on the ground!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto540 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||8
